<!DOCTYPE RCC>
<!--
  The window/taskbar icon, COMPILED INTO the exe.

  It used to be painter-drawn in main.cpp specifically so a portable copy could not lose the file.
  A .qrc keeps that guarantee — the PNG is linked into the binary, not read from disk — while
  letting the icon be a real image rather than something reconstructed with drawPolygon.

  Same artwork as res/app.ico, which the Windows resource (res/app.rc) uses for the FILE icon in
  Explorer and on the desktop. Two mechanisms, one source image; update both together.
-->
<RCC>
    <qresource prefix="/">
        <file>app_256.png</file>
    </qresource>
</RCC>
